## Why This Is Asked

Onboarding flows with email verification and first financial actions are common and require reliable test seeds, deterministic API mocks, and end-to-end coverage across UI and backend interactions.

## Key Concepts

- E2E test planning for signup, verification, and transfer
- Data seeding and test isolation
- Email verification flow simulation (URL interception)
- Network stubs/mocks for deterministic responses
- Balance assertion after transfer

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
test('onboarding with email verify and first transfer', async ({ page }) => {
  await seedTestAccount();
  await page.goto('/signup');
  await page.fill('#email', 'test@example.com');
  await page.fill('#password', 'StrongP@ss1');
  await page.click('#submit');
  await interceptEmailVerification(() => {
    // simulate click on verification link
  });
  await page.fill('#amount', '100');
  await page.click('#transfer');
  await verifyBalanceUpdated(100);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test repeated signup attempts with rate limiting?
- How would you ensure tests remain reliable across test data resets?

